      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Also, assuming this bug were fixed and the player count was correct, I think it's counter productive to show users a categorically lower number on one list than on other lists. \n\nIn every single other list in the world browser you see the total player count. You're conditioned to seeing 50 players in a world and knowing that means that far fewer players are in the public lobbies. Probably only 5 or so in publics.\n\nThen you look at the Games list and see 50 players in a world. In reality, there are 50 players in public lobbies! The total number for that world is probably closer to 500. Had you been browsing another category, you would have seen a much higher number!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
